      reg_item    : "DisableRunAs"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.146 WN22-CC-000530"
      info        : "Windows Server 2022 must have PowerShell Transcription enabled.

GROUP ID: V-254384
RULE ID: SV-254384r958420

Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.

Enabling PowerShell Transcription will record detailed information from the processing of PowerShell commands and scripts. This can provide additional detail when malware has run on a system."
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> Windows PowerShell >> \'Turn on PowerShell Transcription\' to \'Enabled\'

Specify the Transcript output directory to point to a Central Log Server or another secure location to prevent user access.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-171r3|03.03.02a.,800-53|AU-3,800-53r5|AU-3e.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000134,CN-L3|7.1.2.3(a),CN-L3|7.1.2.3(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(b),CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|PR.PS-04,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.28,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ITSG-33|AU-3,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.6.2,NIAv2|AM34a,NIAv2|AM34b,NIAv2|AM34c,NIAv2|AM34d,NIAv2|AM34e,NIAv2|AM34f,NIAv2|AM34g,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.2,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.4,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.5,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.6,PCI-DSSv4.0|10.2.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254384r958420_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-CC-000530,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,Vuln-ID|V-254384"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "1"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\PowerShell\Transcription"
      reg_item    : "EnableTranscripting"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "c:\program files"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "STATUS: PASSED"
          powershell_args : "$f = $env:PROGRAMFILES;
      $acls = (icacls $f);
      $status = 'PASSED';
      foreach ($acl in $acls) {
        if (!$acl) { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*NT SERVICE\TrustedInstaller:*(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*NT SERVICE\TrustedInstaller:*(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM:*(M)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Administrators:*(M)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Administrators:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Users:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Users:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*CREATOR OWNER:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like 'Successfully processed*') { continue }
        $status = 'FAILED'
      }
      $acls;
      '';
      'STATUS: '+$status"
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
