        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Administrators:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Users:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Users:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*CREATOR OWNER:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like 'Successfully processed*') { continue }
        $status = 'FAILED'
      }
      $acls;
      '';
      'STATUS: '+$status"
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.15 WN22-00-000150"
          info        : 'Windows Server 2022 permissions for program file directories must conform to minimum requirements.

GROUP ID: V-254252
RULE ID: SV-254252r958702

Changing the system\'s file and directory permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system and installed applications.

The default permissions are adequate when the Security Option \'Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\' is set to \'Disabled\' (WN22-SO-000240).

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124'
          solution    : 'Maintain the default permissions for the program file directories and configure the Security Option \'Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\' to \'Disabled\' (WN22-SO-000240).

Default permissions:\\Program Files and \\Program Files (x86)Type - \'Allow\' for allInherited from - \'None\' for all

