    <if>
      <condition type:"OR">
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "Check if no administrator accounts exist."
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "No enabled local administrator accounts found."
          powershell_args : '$adminMembers = Get-LocalGroupMember -Group "Administrators" | Where-Object { $_.ObjectClass -eq \'User\' }; $enabledAdmins = foreach ($member in $adminMembers) { $userName = ($member.Name -split \'\\\\\')[-1]; $user = Get-LocalUser -Name $userName; if ($user.Enabled) { $user } }; if ($enabledAdmins) { Write-Host "Enabled local administrator accounts found:"; $enabledAdmins | Format-Table Name, Enabled } else { Write-Host "No enabled local administrator accounts found." }'
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type          : WMI_POLICY
          description   : "Check if server is Standalone"
          value_type    : POLICY_DWORD
          value_data    : "2"
          wmi_namespace : "root/CIMV2"
          wmi_request   : "select DomainRole from Win32_ComputerSystem"
          wmi_attribute : "DomainRole"
          wmi_key       : "DomainRole"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.2 WN22-00-000020"
          info        : "Windows Server 2022 passwords for the built-in Administrator account must be changed at least every 60 days.

GROUP ID: V-254239
RULE ID: SV-254239r1081067

The longer a password is in use, the greater the opportunity for someone to gain unauthorized knowledge of the password. The built-in Administrator account is not generally used and its password may not be changed as frequently as necessary. Changing the password for the built-in Administrator account on a regular basis will limit its exposure.

Windows LAPS must be used to change the built-in Administrator account password."
          solution    : "Change the enabled local Administrator account password at least every 60 days. Windows LAPS must be used to change the built-in Administrator account password. Domain-joined systems can configure this to occur more frequently. LAPS will change the password every 30 days by default.

More information is available at: https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/windows-it-pro-blog/by-popular-demand-windows-laps-available-now/ba-p/3788747 https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/identity/laps/laps-overview#windows-laps-supported-platforms-and-azure-ad-laps-preview-status"
          reference   : "800-171|3.5.2,800-171r3|03.05.07,800-53|IA-5(1),800-53r5|IA-5(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000199,CCI|CCI-004066,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.17,ITSG-33|IA-5(1),LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.2.3,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254239r1081067_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000020,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.1,Vuln-ID|V-254239"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
        </report>
      </then>

      <else>
        <if>
          <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
              description     : "Password last set date for Admin account."
              value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data      : "PASS: Password age within recommended limits"
              powershell_args : '$admin = (Get-LocalUser -Name * | where {$_.Description -eq \'Built-in account for administering the computer/domain\'} | Select-Object *); $pwage = $admin.PasswordLastSet; $threshold = (Get-Date).AddDays(-@ADMIN_REFRESH@); if ([Math]::Abs(($pwage - $threshold).TotalDays) -ge @ADMIN_REFRESH@) {Write-Host(\\"FAIL:\\", $admin.name, \\"password last changed\\", $(if ($pwage) {$pwage} else {\\"never\\"}))} else {Write-Host(\\"PASS: Password age within recommended limits\\")}'
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
              description : "LAPS password age configured."
              value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
              value_data  : "@PASSWORD_AGE@"
              reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\LAPS"
              reg_item    : "PasswordAgeDays"
              reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
              description : "LAPS password length configured."
              value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
              value_data  : "@PASSWORD_LENGTH@"
              reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\LAPS"
              reg_item    : "PasswordLength"
              reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
              description : "LAPS password complexity configured."
              value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
              value_data  : "@PASSWORD_COMPLEXITY@"
              reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\LAPS"
              reg_item    : "PasswordComplexity"
              reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type        : REG_CHECK
              description : "LAPS name of administrator account enabled."
              value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data  : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\LAPS"
              reg_option  : MUST_EXIST
              key_item    : "AdministratorAccountName"
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.2 WN22-00-000020"
              info        : "Windows Server 2022 passwords for the built-in Administrator account must be changed at least every 60 days.

GROUP ID: V-254239
RULE ID: SV-254239r1081067

The longer a password is in use, the greater the opportunity for someone to gain unauthorized knowledge of the password. The built-in Administrator account is not generally used and its password may not be changed as frequently as necessary. Changing the password for the built-in Administrator account on a regular basis will limit its exposure.

Windows LAPS must be used to change the built-in Administrator account password."
              solution    : "Change the enabled local Administrator account password at least every 60 days. Windows LAPS must be used to change the built-in Administrator account password. Domain-joined systems can configure this to occur more frequently. LAPS will change the password every 30 days by default.

More information is available at: https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/windows-it-pro-blog/by-popular-demand-windows-laps-available-now/ba-p/3788747 https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/identity/laps/laps-overview#windows-laps-supported-platforms-and-azure-ad-laps-preview-status"
              reference   : "800-171|3.5.2,800-171r3|03.05.07,800-53|IA-5(1),800-53r5|IA-5(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000199,CCI|CCI-004066,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.17,ITSG-33|IA-5(1),LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.2.3,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254239r1081067_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000020,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.1,Vuln-ID|V-254239"
              see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </then>
        </if>
      </else>
    </if>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type          : WMI_POLICY
          description   : "Check if server is Domain Controller"
          value_type    : POLICY_DWORD
          value_data    : "4" || "5"
          wmi_namespace : "root/CIMV2"
          wmi_request   : "select DomainRole from Win32_ComputerSystem"
          wmi_attribute : "DomainRole"
          wmi_key       : "DomainRole"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type                 : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description          : "1.20 WN22-00-000200"
          info                 : "Windows Server 2022 accounts must require passwords.

GROUP ID: V-254257
RULE ID: SV-254257r958482

The lack of password protection enables anyone to gain access to the information system, which opens a backdoor opportunity for intruders to compromise the system as well as other resources. Accounts on a system must require passwords."
          solution             : 'Configure all enabled accounts to require passwords.

The password required flag can be set by entering the following on a command line:

\'Net user [username] /passwordreq:yes\', substituting [username]

with the name of the user account.'
          reference            : "800-171|3.5.1,800-171r3|03.05.01a.,800-53|IA-2,800-53r5|IA-2,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000764,CN-L3|7.1.3.1(a),CN-L3|7.1.3.1(e),CN-L3|8.1.4.1(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(a),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ITSG-33|IA-2,ITSG-33|IA-2a.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T2.3.8,NESA|T5.3.1,NESA|T5.4.2,NESA|T5.5.1,NESA|T5.5.2,NESA|T5.5.3,NIAv2|AM2,NIAv2|AM8,NIAv2|AM14b,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254257r958482_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000200,TBA-FIISB|35.1,TBA-FIISB|36.1,Vuln-ID|V-254257"
          see_also             : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
          value_type           : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data           : "All users require passwords"
          powershell_args      : '$users = Get-Aduser -Filter \'PasswordNotRequired -eq \\"True\\" -and Enabled -eq \\"True\\" -and SAMAccountType -ne 805306370\' | FT Name, SID; If ($users) { $users } Else { \'All users require passwords\' }'
          only_show_cmd_output : NO
          check_type           : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <custom_item>
          type                 : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description          : "1.20 WN22-00-000200"
          info                 : "Windows Server 2022 accounts must require passwords.

GROUP ID: V-254257
RULE ID: SV-254257r958482

The lack of password protection enables anyone to gain access to the information system, which opens a backdoor opportunity for intruders to compromise the system as well as other resources. Accounts on a system must require passwords."
          solution             : 'Configure all enabled accounts to require passwords.

The password required flag can be set by entering the following on a command line:

\'Net user [username] /passwordreq:yes\', substituting [username]

with the name of the user account.'
          reference            : "800-171|3.5.1,800-171r3|03.05.01a.,800-53|IA-2,800-53r5|IA-2,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000764,CN-L3|7.1.3.1(a),CN-L3|7.1.3.1(e),CN-L3|8.1.4.1(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(a),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ITSG-33|IA-2,ITSG-33|IA-2a.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T2.3.8,NESA|T5.3.1,NESA|T5.4.2,NESA|T5.5.1,NESA|T5.5.2,NESA|T5.5.3,NIAv2|AM2,NIAv2|AM8,NIAv2|AM14b,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254257r958482_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000200,TBA-FIISB|35.1,TBA-FIISB|36.1,Vuln-ID|V-254257"
          see_also             : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
          value_type           : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data           : "All users require passwords"
          powershell_args      : '$users = Get-CimInstance -Class Win32_Useraccount -Filter \\"PasswordRequired=False and LocalAccount=True\\" | Where-Object {$_.Disabled -match \'False\'} | FT Name, PasswordRequired, Disabled, LocalAccount | Format-Table Name, SID; if ($users) { $users } else { \'All users require passwords\' }'
          only_show_cmd_output : NO
          check_type           : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </else>
    </if>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type          : WMI_POLICY
          description   : "Check if server is Member Server"
          value_type    : POLICY_DWORD
          value_data    : "3"
          wmi_namespace : "root/CIMV2"
          wmi_request   : "select DomainRole from Win32_ComputerSystem"
          wmi_attribute : "DomainRole"
          wmi_key       : "DomainRole"
          check_type    : CHECK_EQUAL
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type        : USER_RIGHTS_POLICY
          description : "1.200 WN22-MS-000100"
          info        : 'Windows Server 2022 Deny log on as a service user right on domain-joined member servers must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts. No other groups or accounts must be assigned this right.

GROUP ID: V-254437
RULE ID: SV-254437r958472

Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.

The \'Deny log on as a service\' user right defines accounts that are denied logon as a service.

In an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower-trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.

Incorrect configurations could prevent services from starting and result in a denial of service.'
          solution    : "Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> User Rights Assignment >> Deny log on as a service

to include the following:

Domain systems:

 - Enterprise Admins Group
