    <custom_item>
      type         : CHECK_ACCOUNT
      description  : "1.208 WN22-SO-000010"
      info         : "Windows Server 2022 must have the built-in guest account disabled.

GROUP ID: V-254445
RULE ID: SV-254445r958504

A system faces an increased vulnerability threat if the built-in guest account is not disabled. This is a known account that exists on all Windows systems and cannot be deleted. This account is initialized during the installation of the operating system with no password assigned."
      solution     : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Accounts: Guest account status to \'Disabled\'```.'
      reference    : "800-53|IA-8,800-53r5|IA-8,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000804,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ITSG-33|IA-8,ITSG-33|IA-8a.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T4.3.1,NESA|T5.4.2,NESA|T5.5.1,NESA|T5.5.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254445r958504_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-SO-000010,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.8,Vuln-ID|V-254445"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
      value_type   : POLICY_SET
      value_data   : "Disabled"
      account_type : GUEST_ACCOUNT
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type          : WMI_POLICY
          description   : "Check if server is Domain Controller"
          value_type    : POLICY_DWORD
          value_data    : "4" || "5"
          wmi_namespace : "root/CIMV2"
          wmi_request   : "select DomainRole from Win32_ComputerSystem"
          wmi_attribute : "DomainRole"
          wmi_key       : "DomainRole"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "1.21 WN22-00-000210"
          info            : "Windows Server 2022 passwords must be configured to expire.

GROUP ID:V-254258
RULE ID: SV-254258r1051089

Passwords that do not expire or are reused increase the exposure of a password with greater probability of being discovered or cracked."
          solution        : 'Configure all enabled user account passwords to expire.

Uncheck \'Password never expires\' for all enabled user accounts in Active Directory Users and Computers for domain accounts and Users in Computer Management for member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. Document any exceptions with the information system security officer (ISSO).'
          reference       : "800-171|3.5.2,800-171r3|03.05.07,800-53|IA-5(1),800-53r5|IA-5(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000199,CCI|CCI-004066,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.17,ITSG-33|IA-5(1),LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.2.3,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254258r1051089_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000210,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.1"
          see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "All users passwords expire"
          powershell_args : '$users = Get-Aduser -Filter \'PasswordNeverExpires -eq \\"True\\" -and Enabled -eq \\"True\\" -and SAMAccountType -ne 805306370\' | FT Name, SID; If ($users) { $users } Else { \'All users passwords expire\' }'
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "1.21 WN22-00-000210"
          info            : "Windows Server 2022 passwords must be configured to expire.

GROUP ID:V-254258
RULE ID: SV-254258r1051089

Passwords that do not expire or are reused increase the exposure of a password with greater probability of being discovered or cracked."
          solution        : 'Configure all enabled user account passwords to expire.

Uncheck \'Password never expires\' for all enabled user accounts in Active Directory Users and Computers for domain accounts and Users in Computer Management for member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. Document any exceptions with the information system security officer (ISSO).'
          reference       : "800-171|3.5.2,800-171r3|03.05.07,800-53|IA-5(1),800-53r5|IA-5(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000199,CCI|CCI-004066,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.17,ITSG-33|IA-5(1),LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.2.3,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254258r1051089_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000210,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.1"
          see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "All users passwords expire or are managed by LAPS"
          powershell_args : '$LAPSAccount=(Get-ItemProperty \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).AdministratorAccountName;if($LAPSAccount){$LAPSAccount=$LAPSAccount.Trim()}else{$builtinAdmin=Get-LocalUser|Where-Object{$_.SID.Value -match \'-500$\'};if($builtinAdmin){$LAPSAccount=$builtinAdmin.Name.Trim()}};$users=Get-LocalUser|Where-Object{(($_.PasswordExpires -eq $null)-or($_.PasswordExpires -eq $false))-and($_.Enabled -eq $true)-and(($LAPSAccount-and($_.Name.Trim() -ne $LAPSAccount))-or(-not $LAPSAccount))};if($users){$users|Select-Object Name,SID}else{\'All users passwords expire or are managed by LAPS\'}'
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </else>
    </if>

    <custom_item>
      type         : CHECK_ACCOUNT
      description  : "1.210 WN22-SO-000030"
      info         : "Windows Server 2022 built-in administrator account must be renamed.

GROUP ID: V-254447
RULE ID: SV-254447r991589

The built-in administrator account is a well-known account subject to attack. Renaming this account to an unidentified name improves the protection of this account and the system."
      solution     : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Accounts: Rename administrator account

to a name other than \'Administrator\'.'
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-254447r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-SO-000030,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-254447"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
      value_type   : POLICY_TEXT
      value_data   : "Administrator"
      account_type : ADMINISTRATOR_ACCOUNT
      check_type   : CHECK_NOT_EQUAL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type         : CHECK_ACCOUNT
      description  : "1.211 WN22-SO-000040"
      info         : "Windows Server 2022 built-in guest account must be renamed.

GROUP ID: V-254448
RULE ID: SV-254448r991589

The built-in guest account is a well-known user account on all Windows systems and, as initially installed, does not require a password. This can allow access to system resources by unauthorized users. Renaming this account to an unidentified name improves the protection of this account and the system."
      solution     : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Accounts: Rename guest account

to a name other than \'Guest\'.'
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-254448r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-SO-000040,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-254448"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
      value_type   : POLICY_TEXT
      value_data   : "Guest"
      account_type : GUEST_ACCOUNT
      check_type   : CHECK_NOT_EQUAL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.212 WN22-SO-000050"
      info        : "Windows Server 2022 must force audit policy subcategory settings to override audit policy category settings.

GROUP ID: V-254449
RULE ID: SV-254449r958442

Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior. This setting allows administrators to enable more precise auditing capabilities."
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings to \'Enabled\''
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-171r3|03.03.03a.,800-53|AU-12a.,800-53r5|AU-12a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000169,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|DE.CM-3,CSF|DE.CM-7,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-01,CSF2.0|DE.CM-03,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-04,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ITSG-33|AU-12a.,LEVEL|2A,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.1,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-254449r958442_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-SO-000050,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,Vuln-ID|V-254449"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "1"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa"
      reg_item    : "SCENoApplyLegacyAuditPolicy"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.213 WN22-SO-000060"
      info        : "Windows Server 2022 setting Domain member: Digitally encrypt or sign secure channel data (always) must be configured to Enabled.

GROUP ID: V-254450
RULE ID: SV-254450r958908

Requests sent on the secure channel are authenticated, and sensitive information (such as passwords) is encrypted, but not all information is encrypted. If this policy is enabled, outgoing secure channel traffic will be encrypted and signed.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188"
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Domain member: Digitally encrypt or sign secure channel data (always) to \'Enabled\''
