    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.239 WN22-SO-000320"
      info        : 'Windows Server 2022 must be configured to at least negotiate signing for LDAP client signing.

GROUP ID: V-254476
RULE ID: SV-254476r991589

This setting controls the signing requirements for LDAP clients. This must be set to \'Negotiate signing\' or \'Require signing\', depending on the environment and type of LDAP server in use.'
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Network security: LDAP client signing requirements to \'Negotiate signing\' at a minimum'
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-254476r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-SO-000320,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-254476"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "1"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LDAP"
      reg_item    : "LDAPClientIntegrity"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "1.24 WN22-00-000240"
      info        : "Windows Server 2022 must have software certificate installation files removed.

GROUP ID: V-254261
RULE ID: SV-254261r991589

Use of software certificates and their accompanying installation files for end users to access resources is less secure than the use of hardware-based certificates.

NOTE: Nessus has not performed this check. Please review the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "Remove any certificate installation files (*.p12 and *.pfx) found on a system.

Note: This does not apply to server-based applications that have a requirement for .p12 certificate files or Adobe PreFlight certificate files."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-254261r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000240,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-254261"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
    </report>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.240 WN22-SO-000330"
