          description    : "1.48 WN22-AC-000010"
          info           : "Windows Server 2022 account lockout duration must be configured to 15 minutes or greater.

GROUP ID: V-254285
RULE ID: SV-254285r958736

The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. This parameter specifies the period of time that an account will remain locked after the specified number of failed logon attempts."
          solution       : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Account Lockout Policy >> Account lockout duration to \'15\' minutes or greater

A value of \'0\' is also acceptable, requiring an administrator to unlock the account.'
          reference      : "800-171|3.1.8,800-171r3|03.01.08b.,800-53|AC-7b.,800-53r5|AC-7b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002238,CN-L3|7.1.2.7(f),CN-L3|7.1.3.1(c),CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.5,ITSG-33|AC-7b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T5.5.1,NIAv2|AM24,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.7,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.3.4,Rule-ID|SV-254285r958736_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-AC-000010,TBA-FIISB|36.2.4,TBA-FIISB|45.1.2,Vuln-ID|V-254285"
          see_also       : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
          value_type     : TIME_MINUTE
          value_data     : "[15..MAX]" || "0"
          lockout_policy : LOCKOUT_DURATION
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"FAILED">
