    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type          : WMI_POLICY
          description   : "Check if server is Standalone"
          value_type    : POLICY_DWORD
          value_data    : "2"
          wmi_namespace : "root/CIMV2"
          wmi_request   : "select DomainRole from Win32_ComputerSystem"
          wmi_attribute : "DomainRole"
          wmi_key       : "DomainRole"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.9 WN22-00-000090"
          info        : "Windows Server 2022 domain-joined systems must have a Trusted Platform Module (TPM) enabled and ready for use.

GROUP ID: V-254246
RULE ID: SV-254246r991589

Credential Guard uses virtualization-based security to protect data that could be used in credential theft attacks if compromised. A number of system requirements must be met in order for Credential Guard to be configured and enabled properly. Without a TPM enabled and ready for use, Credential Guard keys are stored in a less secure method using software."
          solution    : 'Ensure domain-joined systems have a TPM that is configured for use. (Versions 2.0 or 1.2 support Credential Guard.)

The TPM must be enabled in the firmware.

Run \'tpm.msc\' for configuration options in Windows.'
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-254246r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000090,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-254246"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
        </report>
      </then>

      <else>
        <if>
          <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
              description     : "TpmPresent"
              value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data      : "TpmPresent : True"
              powershell_args : "Get-Tpm | select 'TpmPresent' | Format-List"
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
              description     : "TpmReady"
              value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data      : "TpmReady : True"
              powershell_args : "Get-Tpm | select 'TpmReady' | Format-List"
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.9 WN22-00-000090"
              info        : "Windows Server 2022 domain-joined systems must have a Trusted Platform Module (TPM) enabled and ready for use.

GROUP ID: V-254246
RULE ID: SV-254246r991589

Credential Guard uses virtualization-based security to protect data that could be used in credential theft attacks if compromised. A number of system requirements must be met in order for Credential Guard to be configured and enabled properly. Without a TPM enabled and ready for use, Credential Guard keys are stored in a less secure method using software."
              solution    : 'Ensure domain-joined systems have a TPM that is configured for use. (Versions 2.0 or 1.2 support Credential Guard.)

The TPM must be enabled in the firmware.

Run \'tpm.msc\' for configuration options in Windows.'
              reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-254246r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN22-00-000090,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-254246"
              see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22357"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </then>
        </if>
      </else>
    </if>

